    {
      "id": "calculus-2-1:improper-integral",
      "type": "single_choice",
      "prompt": "Which of the following improper integrals converges to a finite value?",
      "options": [
        "∫ from 1 to ∞ of 1 dx",
        "∫ from 1 to ∞ of x⁻² dx",
        "∫ from 1 to ∞ of x⁻¹ dx",
        "∫ from 1 to ∞ of x⁻¹ᐟ² dx"
      ],
      "points": 1,
      "objective_ids": [
        "calculus-2-1-objective-2"
      ],
      "solution_spec": {
        "answer": 1
      },
      "feedback": {
        "hint": "Use the p-test: ∫ from 1 to ∞ of x⁻ᵖ dx converges if and only if p > 1.",
        "solution": "With p = 2 the antiderivative −1/x gives the value 1, so the integral converges. For p = 1 and p = 1/2 the antiderivative grows without bound, and a constant integrand grows linearly, so those diverge.",
        "lesson_ids": [
          "calculus-2-1"
        ],
        "misconception_ids": []
      },
      "visibility": "public-practice-authoring",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "original",
        "modifications": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "calculus-2-2:taylor-remainder",
      "type": "numeric",
      "prompt": "The degree-2 Taylor polynomial of eˣ at 0 is used to estimate e^0.5. Use the Lagrange remainder bound |R₂| ≤ M|x|³/3! with M = e^0.5 ≈ 1.6487 to bound the error. Enter a number.",
      "points": 1,
      "objective_ids": [
        "calculus-2-2-objective-2"
      ],
      "solution_spec": {
        "answer": 0.0343,
        "unit": "",
        "tolerance": 0.0005,
        "unit_required": false,
        "significant_figures": null,
        "dimensions": null
      },
      "feedback": {
        "hint": "On [0, 0.5] the third derivative of eˣ is at most e^0.5.",
        "solution": "|R₂| ≤ 1.6487 × 0.5³ ÷ 6 = 0.0343. The polynomial gives 1.625, and the true value 1.6487 differs by 0.0237, which is inside the bound.",
        "lesson_ids": [
          "calculus-2-2"
        ],
        "misconception_ids": []
      },
      "visibility": "public-practice-authoring",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "original",
        "modifications": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "calculus-2-3:variable-force-work",
      "type": "numeric",
      "prompt": "A spring-like force F(x) = 4x newtons acts along a displacement from x = 0 to x = 3 m. Calculate the work done. Enter a value and unit.",
      "points": 1,
      "objective_ids": [
        "calculus-2-3-objective-2"
      ],
      "solution_spec": {
        "answer": 18.0,
        "unit": "J",
        "tolerance": 0.05,
        "unit_required": true,
        "significant_figures": null,
        "dimensions": null
      },
      "feedback": {
        "hint": "Integrate the force over the displacement.",
        "solution": "W = ∫₀³ 4x dx = 2x² evaluated from 0 to 3 = 18 N·m = 18 J. The units come from newtons times meters.",
        "lesson_ids": [
          "calculus-2-3"
        ],
        "misconception_ids": []
      },
      "visibility": "public-practice-authoring",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "original",
        "modifications": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "calculus-2-4:alternating-series-error",
